# Holdout evaluation set stays OUT of the repo on purpose. Once it is
# committed it is visible to every future change, and a holdout that anyone
# can read while tuning stops being a holdout. Decision 2026-08-15.
holdout_samples.json
holdout-evaluation-report.html
scrubber-options-for-management.html

# Synthetic verification batch (2026-08-15). Same reasoning as the holdout:
# an evaluation set that is visible while tuning stops measuring anything.
# Provenance and limitations are in the file's own _provenance block --
# it is Claude-authored, so its number is a verification-batch figure and
# never the holdout figure.
eval_samples_v2.json
holdout_v3.json

# Session review documents (2026-08-16). Same reasoning as the evaluation
# sets: they quote scrubbed output and sample IDs from gitignored holdout
# files, and a holdout anyone can read while tuning stops being a holdout.
# The text is elided and the repo is private, so the fragments already in
# commits d333f23 and earlier are ACCEPTED and history is NOT rewritten --
# but the standard applied to test_jargon.py (paraphrase, never the sample
# text) applies here too, and this restores consistency with it.
REVIEW-*.md
